26074.9s 147 
26074.9s 148 The paper used its own data; our numbers are on the 498R All-in-One test split (different data),
26074.9s 149 so the comparison shows the direction and size of the gap, not a head-to-head result.
26074.9s 150 
26074.9s 151 The paper's Table 2 is Ultralytics' own COCO table (the paper runs no experiment of its own); its speed column is model-only TensorRT, ours is pre + inference + post at batch 1. In Ultralytics 8.4.170 a YOLO26 model runs its one-to-many head with NMS unless `nms=False` is given: the training runs (y26n, y26s, ...) are scored that way, the heads_* runs score both heads of the same weights.
